+++
title: The awkward cases
+++
% // A site made of the inputs that are easy to get wrong.
% //
% // Every one of these passes a unit test against an engine that still builds
% // the wrong SITE: what they exercise is identity, ordering and the walk,
% // which only a whole build shows. check-sites builds the lot both ways and
% // diffs; each line below says what its file is for.
%
% // A .yaml whose first line is `---` must not be read as a document
% // separator, and an empty or whitespace-only .mdy must not shift every
% // later document by one. If either is wrong, `city.yaml`'s fields land on
% // some other file's record and this query answers with the wrong one — or
% // with nothing.
% const cities = $.find({ role: "city" })
% $.emit("cities.json", JSON.stringify(cities.map((c) => c.who + "/" + c.era)))
%
% // A file name carrying a `"` is deliberately NOT here: Windows forbids a
% // quote in a file name, so committing one would break the checkout on a
% // platform this project builds for. test/engine.c covers it by making the
% // file at run time in a temp directory, which is the only way to test it on
% // a repository that has to clone everywhere.
%
% // The `+++` inside a block scalar is data, not a front-matter marker.
% const notes = $.find({ kind: "note" })
% $.emit("note.json", JSON.stringify(notes.map((n) => n.body)))
%
% // A .md reached through $.render, and the same document through $.text —
% // the two halves of that path.
% $.emit("prose.html", $.render({ path: "pages/prose.md" }))
% $.emit("prose.txt", $.text({ path: "pages/prose.md" }))
%
% // A table of seventy columns, which no fixed-size cell array survives.
% $.emit("wide.html", $.render({ path: "pages/wide.md" }))
%
% // A tight list item holding a BLOCK — a quote, a fence, a heading, a table,
% // or text followed by one. Each gets a newline before it and after the
% // last, which is mdast-util-to-hast's listItem rather than the wrap(loose)
% // every other block parent takes.
% $.emit("nested.html", $.render({ path: "pages/nested.md" }))
%
% // GFM footnotes in a .md: numbering by first reference, a repeat's -2, a
% // reference in a table cell (md4c counts those twice), and a definition
% // with nothing in it.
% $.emit("notes.html", $.render({ path: "pages/notes.md" }))
%
% // Raw HTML INSIDE a paragraph, where node writes the markup rather than
% // escaping it — the block kind is the easy half. Also the two places a tag
% // must STAY literal: a code span and an image's alt.
% $.emit("raw.html", $.render({ path: "pages/raw.md" }))
%
% // A .tif whose header points its IFD past the end of the file. It is a real
% // file and still gets a record; what it must not get is width/height read
% // from off the end of it.
% const img = $.findOne({ ext: ".tif" })
% $.emit("image.json", JSON.stringify({ name: img.name, w: img.width ?? null, h: img.height ?? null }))
%
% // The whole set, in order — what a desynchronised walk moves.
% $.emit("order.json", JSON.stringify($.find({}).map((d) => d.path)))

= {{ res.data.title }}

{{ cities.length }} city, {{ $.count }} documents.
